MIT OR Apache-2.0: its books are MoneyKeep books.

The user interface is built with Slint (https://slint.dev), used under the Slint
Royalty-free Desktop, Mobile, and Web Applications License 2.0 (its text is in
THIRD-PARTY-LICENSES.txt, with the slint crates); the README shows Slint's
attribution badge, as that licence asks. Form1099Keep does not redistribute Slint
on its own. Form1099Keep's own code stays MIT OR Apache-2.0.

Every third-party crate compiled into Form1099Keep is listed with its version,
its licence and the licence texts it ships in THIRD-PARTY-LICENSES.txt, installed
beside the programs.

Form1099Keep prepares Forms 1099-NEC and 1099-MISC; it does not give tax advice
or transmit to the IRS.
